<section id="view-method" class="view" hidden>
  <h2>How the numbers are made</h2>
  <div class="method-grid">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>The formula</h3>
      <p class="formula" id="formula"></p>
      <p id="formulaText"></p>
      <h3>The filter</h3>
      <p id="filterText"></p>
      <h3>The farm verdict</h3>
      <p>The airdrop pool is taken as 10% of the implied value, shared pro-rata across TVL, so a $1,000 ticket earns implied &times; 0.10 &times; 1,000 / TVL. Gas is priced per transaction by the protocol's main chain (Ethereum $12, Base/Arbitrum/Optimism/Blast $1, Solana/Polygon/Sui/Aptos $0.10, BNB/Avalanche/Fantom/Tron $0.50, anything else $2), named with the chain's gas token where it is a settled fact (ETH, SOL, POL, SUI, APT, BNB, AVAX, FTM, TRX, HYPE, MON), and multiplied by the plan's transaction count: setup, one a week through the hold, and the claim. <strong>FARM</strong> if the net is $25 or more, <strong>THIN</strong> if it is $0 or more, <strong>SKIP</strong> if the drop does not cover the gas.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Out-of-sample proof</h3>
      <table class="proof" id="proofTable">
        <thead><tr><th>Check</th><th class="num">This board</th><th class="num">Flat multiple</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Leave-one-out refits the model once per traded token, holding one out each time. Walk-forward fits only the older half of the dated traded tokens and tests the newer half. The flat multiple is the median market-cap-to-TVL ratio of the traded tokens, the simplest rule that prices on TVL alone. The curve beats it on both checks, and on the share of tokens predicted within 3&times;.</p>
      <h3>Tenure, tested and not priced</h3>
      <p>How long a protocol has run with no token was tested as a term in the value model in five forms, each fitted on the residual after curve, category and growth, its contribution clamped to &plusmn;0.15 like growth; protocols with no listed date are left out of the fit (they take zero when priced). None of them earns its place:</p>
      <table class="proof" id="tenureTable">
        <thead><tr><th>Tenure form</th><th class="num">Fitted slope</th><th class="num">Leave-one-out</th><th class="num">Walk-forward</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>No tenure (this board)</td><td class="num">&mdash;</td><td class="num">&times;2.96 (51%)</td><td class="num">&times;2.26 (62%)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>log10(age in days)</td><td class="num">&minus;0.0304</td><td class="num">&times;3.14 (48%)</td><td class="num">&times;2.94 (51%)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>log10(age, capped 365d)</td><td class="num">+0.2197</td><td class="num">&times;3.22 (47%)</td><td class="num">&times;2.26 (62%)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>log10(age, capped 730d)</td><td class="num">&minus;0.1735</td><td class="num">&times;3.22 (46%)</td><td class="num">&times;2.26 (62%)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>&radic;(age in years)</td><td class="num">&minus;0.0155</td><td class="num">&times;3.14 (49%)</td><td class="num">&times;2.35 (62%)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Age buckets (&lt;1y / 1&ndash;3y / &gt;3y)</td><td class="num">+0.068 / &minus;0.018 / +0.047</td><td class="num">&times;3.04 (49%)</td><td class="num">&times;2.18 (59%)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Every form worsens leave-one-out. The slope's sign flips across forms (&minus;0.03 uncapped, +0.22 capped at 365 days, &minus;0.17 capped at 730), and the capped-365 slope is carried by 8 young protocols: noise, not signal. The one form whose walk-forward median is a touch better (buckets) has near-zero, non-monotonic offsets and a worse within-3&times; share. So the model does not price age. Age still matters in this board: it sets each farm plan's hold length, which is a different question from what a launch is worth.</p>
      <h3>Enrichment signals, tested and not priced (v3)</h3>
      <p>Fees, longer TVL growth, drawdown and raises were reconstructed point-in-time to 14 Nov 2026 from DefiLlama history and tested the same way as tenure: a fitted term on the residual, clamped to &plusmn;0.15. Adoption needed leave-one-out under &times;2.75 <em>and</em> walk-forward under &times;2.26 <em>and</em> slopes stable across categories. Nothing passed, so the model stays radar-3:</p>
      <table class="proof" id="experimentTable">
        <thead><tr><th>Signal tested</th><th class="num">Fitted slope</th><th class="num">Leave-one-out</th><th class="num">Walk-forward</th><th>Decision</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody></tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Why fees fail: the fitted slope on log annualized fees is &minus;0.0050 — essentially zero once TVL is in the model — and the fees slope flips sign across categories (DEX &minus;0.37, Lending &minus;0.15, Liquid Staking +0.06, RWA &minus;0.05, Yield +0.25). Fees track TVL, so they add no new information about market cap. The P/S ratio (market cap / annualized fees) across the 74 comps with fees has a median of 5.7&times; but spans 0.09&times; to 430,762&times; — far too wide to price with. Growth 90d comes closest (leave-one-out &times;2.90, walk-forward &times;2.13) but misses the &times;2.75 bar, so it stays out too. Dev activity was not fitted at all: only 6 of 104 comps map to an exact repository in the Electric Capital taxonomy, too thin to test honestly.</p>
